      "caveat": "Endometrial carcinoma molecular classification (TCGA 2013 / ProMisE / WHO 2020) (TCGA, Nature 2013; Talhouk et al., ProMisE, Br J Cancer 2015; WHO Classification of Female Genital Tumours, 5th ed. 2020), applied per patient over all their samples, in this order, first match wins: POLE-ultramutated — a somatic POLE exonuclease-domain hotspot called in any sample (P286R, S297F, F367S, F367V, V411L, L424I, L424V, P436R, M444K, A456P, S459F, M295R, D368Y; León-Castillo et al. 2020); else MMR-deficient — MSI-high in any sample by MSI_SENSOR_SCORE (MSIsensor; ≥ 10 MSI-high, < 3 stable) (from the MSI call, not mismatch-repair immunohistochemistry, which the warehouse does not hold); else p53-abnormal — a TP53 mutation the OncoKB store (v7.5) calls oncogenic or likely oncogenic (a sequencing proxy for p53 immunohistochemistry); else NSMP. A patient is “not classifiable”, never put in a subtype by guess, when an input the hierarchy needs before reaching their subtype is missing: not sequenced, not profiled for POLE or TP53 (panel-aware), or no MSI-high or stable call (an indeterminate or unreported MSI result counts as none) — 38 patients here (no MSI call 26, not sequenced 12), kept out of the shares, tests and curves. Shares are of classified patients. By SUBTYPE per patient (“Multiple” when samples disagree; the 8 largest groups drawn, the rest pooled into a named Other), chi-squared over group × subtype per cohort, patients without a value left out of the test. Overall survival by subtype from OS_MONTHS / OS_STATUS as the study records them (for each cohort), Kaplan–Meier with a k-group log-rank; OS is not corrected for left truncation (a patient sequenced years after diagnosis entered the study alive), and the subtypes differ in stage, histology and treatment, none adjusted for. A panel-based call is not the clinical assay: POLE variants outside the hotspot list, MSI by IHC, and p53 IHC patterns are not seen. "
